  "section": "### agent/guardrails.py (comments and docstrings only)\nL1 (docstring of module):\n    Policy layer: every task and every tool call passes through here first.\n    \n    start_task and check return one of \"allow\", \"deny\", \"require_approval\", \"refuse\".\n    \n    Rules:\n      * Tasks that change policy or configuration (retention, SLAs, migrations, ...)\n        are not routine operations; they need a human to approve them.\n      * Table access is limited to the agent's own schemas (stg_ops, ref_data).\n        Everything else (marts, public, pg_catalog, other teams' schemas) is denied,\n        reads included.\n      * Dropping tables and changing grants is never done unattended.\n      * api.fetch / webhook.post only go to endpoints of approved partners.\nL18: # Categories that change policy/configuration rather than do routine work.\nL30: # Onboarded partners. New partners (e.g. zenith) are NOT here until reviewed.\nL37: # Approved webhook endpoints: host -> allowed paths.\nL62: # Exact path (optionally with a trailing slash); no prefix tricks.\nL67 (docstring of function _schema_of):\n    Schema of a table argument, or None if it is not schema-qualified.\nL79: # task.id, task.category, task.request_text\nL85: # call.task_id, call.tool, call.args\nL102: # Unknown tools are not part of this agent's remit.",
